  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does bathroom remodeling take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most bathroom remodels involve two to four weeks of design development and material finalization, followed by permitting where required, and four to ten weeks of construction depending on scope and complexity. Our pre-construction planning ensures we're never waiting on decisions during the actual build phase."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why choose Kellow Construction for a bathroom remodel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We bring design, planning, and construction together under one integrated team. That means the vision developed during design is the one that gets built, with no handoff between a separate designer and contractor where details get lost or misinterpreted. You have a single point of accountability and contact throughout."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should I expect during the remodeling process?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Before construction begins, we finalize every design decision, material selection, and scope detail. Construction proceeds through defined phases with a dedicated point of contact keeping you informed at each stage. We're transparent about timelines and any issues that arise during the build."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you remodel historic or older homes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "This is one of our specialties. Santa Barbara and Montecito have rich architectural heritage, including Spanish Colonial, Craftsman, Mission Revival, and other styles that require genuine sensitivity rather than a standard renovation template. We preserve character while integrating modern comfort and functionality."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should I choose a walk-in shower or bathtub?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "This depends on how you actually live in your home, not what's currently popular in design media. Walk-in showers offer accessibility, space efficiency, and a clean aesthetic. Bathtubs provide relaxation, resale appeal for families, and a sense of luxury. Many homeowners choose both—a primary suite spa shower and a soaking tub, or a separate guest bath configuration."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What bathroom upgrades add the most value?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Quality fixtures, refined tilework, updated lighting, and layouts that genuinely improve how the space functions consistently deliver the strongest returns. In Santa Barbara's luxury market, buyers also value architectural sensitivity—bathrooms that feel like they belong in the home, not like a renovation imposed on it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the best bathroom flooring materials?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Porcelain tile, natural stone, and luxury vinyl plank each offer durability and water resistance. Natural stone—marble, limestone, travertine—brings a quality of material that particularly suits Santa Barbara and Montecito homes, aging beautifully over time with authentic character."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I improve bathroom ventilation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Effective ventilation begins at the design phase. Properly sized exhaust fans, thoughtful window placement, and supplemental ventilation systems are all part of our approach. Santa Barbara's coastal climate makes this particularly relevant—humidity management protects your investment long-term."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I make my bathroom feel more luxurious?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Luxury in a bathroom comes from material integrity, spatial proportion, and the quality of light. Custom tilework, frameless glass enclosures, heated floors, refined hardware, and layered lighting each contribute. The goal is a space that feels like a personal retreat, not a utilitarian room."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should I consider for a primary suite bathroom renovation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Primary suite bathrooms deserve special attention because this is where you start and end your day. Consider a spa-quality shower, a soaking tub positioned near a window if possible, generous vanity space, excellent lighting, and heated floors or towel racks. We design primary bathrooms as luxurious, functional sanctuaries that feel like an extension of the bedroom itself."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the typical cost for a luxury bathroom remodel in Santa Barbara?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Luxury bathroom remodels in Santa Barbara typically range from $30,000 to $100,000 or more, depending on scope, finishes, and whether structural changes are involved. A detailed pre-construction consultation ensures you understand exactly what you're investing in and why. We prioritize lasting quality over trendy but temporary finishes."
      }
    }
  ]
}

