      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the design-build process for whole home remodeling?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We develop a comprehensive design, finalize material selections and structural decisions, and create a detailed construction plan before breaking ground. This integrated approach keeps architects, designers, and construction teams aligned from start to finish."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I stay in my home during a whole home renovation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Strategic phasing and protective measures make it possible in many cases. We complete sections of the home in phases, ensuring functional living areas remain available while construction progresses."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What areas of the home provide the best return on investment?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Kitchens and primary bathrooms consistently return 60-80% of their investment in resale value, while thoughtfully executed whole-home renovations can return 70-90%. Architectural sensitivity and durability are especially important in Santa Barbara homes."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you handle unexpected discoveries during construction?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
