      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I prioritize which rooms to remodel first?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most homeowners begin with the kitchen because of its impact on daily life and resale value, followed by primary bathrooms and secondary living spaces. We help create a strategic sequence that minimizes disruption."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between a renovation and a remodel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A renovation updates finishes and systems without significantly altering the home's layout, while a remodel reconfigures spaces and may involve structural changes. Both can preserve architectural character while improving functionality."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Kellow handle project management?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We assign a dedicated project manager who coordinates trades, schedules, inspections, and communication. You have a single point of contact throughout the project."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What materials work best for whole home renovations?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Material selection depends on architectural style, climate, and durability goals. We often recommend natural stone, quality tile, solid hardwoods, and timeless finishes that age gracefully and complement the home's character."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I maintain my home's architectural integrity during renovation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Start by respecting the original architectural style and ensuring new elements complement it. We preserve significant details when appropriate and design additions that feel intentional and cohesive with the existing home."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should be included in a whole home remodeling contract?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A comprehensive contract should include a detailed scope of work, material specifications, timeline, budget, contingency allowances, warranty information, and communication expectations."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I prepare for a whole home remodel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Prepare by organizing temporary living arrangements if needed, securing belongings in work areas, arranging deliveries, and planning for disruptions. We provide a pre-construction guide to help homeowners prepare."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you handle structural changes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Structural modifications are carefully planned and coordinated with engineers and building officials. We manage all calculations, permits, inspections, and approvals before construction begins."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the biggest challenge in whole home remodeling?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Maintaining alignment with the original vision while adapting to discoveries made during construction is often the greatest challenge. Thorough pre-construction planning helps minimize unexpected issues and keeps the project on track."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does the planning phase take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The planning phase typically takes two to four months and includes design development, material selection, engineering, permitting, and approvals. Investing time upfront reduces delays during construction."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What makes Kellow the right choice for whole home remodeling?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We combine design expertise, construction knowledge, and project management under one roof. Our team understands Santa Barbara's architectural heritage, permitting requirements, and the importance of long-term quality and accountability."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you approach phased renovations for occupied homes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We create a phased construction strategy that keeps essential living spaces functional while work progresses in stages. Dust control, scheduling, and communication are carefully managed to minimize disruption."
      }
    }
  ]
